  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Railways are one of the most important and efficient means of land transport.
    They are widely used to carry large numbers of passengers and heavy goods over
    both short and long distances. Railway transport plays an important role in connecting
    villages, towns, cities, industrial areas, and different regions of a country.

    A
    train usually consists of an engine and a number of coaches or wagons. The engine
    is the main power unit of the train. It provides the force required to pull the
    train along the railway tracks. Passenger coaches are designed to carry people
    comfortably, while goods wagons are used to transport materials such as food
    products, machinery, fuel, raw materials, and other heavy items.

    Railway
    tracks provide a fixed path for the train. The wheels of the train move along
    these tracks, helping the train travel in a controlled and stable direction.
    Tracks are connected through a large railway network that allows trains to travel
    between different stations and destinations.

    Railway stations are important
    points along a railway route. They provide places where trains can stop so passengers
    can board or leave the train. Stations may also include platforms, waiting areas,
    ticket counters, shelters, and other facilities for passengers. Goods can also
    be loaded and unloaded at special railway stations or terminals.

    Railway
    signals are used to control train movement and improve safety. Signals give important
    instructions to train drivers, such as when to stop, wait, or proceed. Red, yellow,
    and green signal lights are commonly used to communicate different conditions
    along the railway line. These signals help maintain safe distances between trains
    and reduce the risk of accidents.

    Railway bridges are built where tracks
    need to cross rivers, roads, valleys, or other obstacles. They provide a strong
    and safe path for trains and help railway routes continue across difficult terrain.
    Bridges are an important part of railway infrastructure.

    Railway routes
    connect different stations through a planned network of tracks. These routes
    make it possible for passengers and goods to travel efficiently from one place
    to another. Large railway networks support trade, tourism, daily travel, and
    the movement of essential materials across different regions.

    Railways are
    especially useful because trains can carry many passengers and large quantities
    of goods at the same time. They are an important part of transportation systems
    and help support economic activity, communication, and regional development.
    By combining engines, coaches, tracks, stations, signals, bridges, and route
    networks, railways provide an organized and reliable way to transport people
    and goods.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
